# Think on a site update

When the user asks for a site update, decide what the person is trying to learn. Ship the line that changes the bet. A fact they can already read on FanDuel, ESPN, or a depth chart is not the update.

Never ship copy that only restates public knowledge:

- "Charbonnet is back for his first game."
- "Front 4-3. Allowed 6 rushing TDs. Linebackers Devin Bush, T.J. Edwards."
- "Seahawks projected 3.5 TDs, 9.4 red zone plays a game."

Everyone can see that the starter is active, what front the defense plays, and the team's projection. None of it says whether the price is wrong.

Say what changed about this bet. Wilson's scores came while he had Charbonnet's carries. Charbonnet has those carries tonight. That is the read. The front, the touchdowns allowed, and the linebackers do not belong on that card.

Before finishing, read the new sentence the way the user will. If it does not change the bet, delete it and write the one that does.
